---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ConceptImage from '../../components/ConceptImage.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Kitchen & Bathroom Renovations in North Alabama"
  description="Explore kitchen and bathroom renovation planning in North Alabama. Discuss layout, storage, materials, and budget priorities with Apex Property Renovation."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Renovations / Kitchens & bathrooms"
    title="Everyday rooms. Thoughtfully reimagined."
    description="The kitchen where the day gathers. The bathroom where it begins. Shape your renovation around the way these rooms need to work, then consider how you want them to feel."
    image="/assets/kitchen-concept.webp"
    alt="AI-generated kitchen renovation concept featuring wood cabinetry and a light stone island"
  >
    <a class="button button-gold" href="/start-your-project/">Start your project <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="kitchen-bath-function">
    <div class="wrap split-content">
      <ConceptImage src="/assets/bath-concept.webp" alt="AI-generated bathroom concept with a warm wood vanity and restrained natural finishes" />
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Function before finish</span>
        <h2 id="kitchen-bath-function">Beautiful is only<br />part of the brief.</h2>
        <p>A kitchen or bathroom renovation in North Alabama should begin with everyday friction. Tell Apex Property Renovation about crowded work surfaces, awkward storage, difficult cleaning, or a layout that no longer fits your household.</p>
        <p>For kitchens, your ideas might include cabinetry, countertops, lighting, flooring, or appliance placement. For bathrooms, describe vanity storage, bathing preferences, tile, fixtures, and ease of use. These examples guide the conversation; the property's condition and a scope assessment determine what is appropriate.</p>
        <p>Considering these rooms within a larger update? Explore <a class="text-link" href="/renovations/whole-home/">whole-home renovations</a> to think through connected finishes and sequencing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-stone" aria-labelledby="kitchen-bath-decisions">
    <div class="wrap split-content">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Choose with intention</span>
        <h2 id="kitchen-bath-decisions">Materials matter.<br />So do the details behind them.</h2>
        <p>A reference image describes a look. A useful project brief also explains maintenance expectations, storage needs, and budget boundaries.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul class="list-lines">
          <li><strong>Layout changes.</strong> Keeping or moving fixtures and appliances can lead to very different scopes. Existing conditions need review before new arrangements are assumed possible.</li>
          <li><strong>Material selections.</strong> Cabinet construction, surface choices, tile formats, and fixture specifications influence both cost and care. Compare practical suitability alongside appearance.</li>
          <li><strong>Hidden conditions.</strong> Areas behind existing finishes may need further attention. Discuss how discoveries and proposed scope changes will be documented and approved.</li>
          <li><strong>Selection timing.</strong> Product availability and lead times can affect the order of work. Early decisions help make coordination more realistic, without assuming a fixed schedule.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="kitchen-bath-faq">
    <div class="wrap split-content">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Kitchen &amp; bathroom questions</span>
        <h2 id="kitchen-bath-faq">Before you choose the tile.</h2>
        <p>For a rental property, see how <a class="text-link" href="/renovations/investment-properties/">investment renovation planning</a> puts durability and repeatable selections first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need to choose every material first?</summary>
          <p>No. Share examples of the look you prefer and the features you need. A shortlist is useful, but final selections should follow a discussion of scope, suitability, availability, and budget rather than precede it.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What drives kitchen and bathroom renovation costs?</summary>
          <p>Room size is only one factor. Cabinetry, surfaces, fixtures, layout changes, preparation, and existing conditions all influence pricing. An assessment is needed before a project-specific estimate; a photograph alone cannot establish a reliable total.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How should I plan for the room being unavailable?</summary>
          <p>Tell us whether you have another bathroom or an alternative food-preparation area. The proposed sequence, access needs, and material availability should inform your arrangements. There is no standard downtime that applies to every renovation.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA title="Make the everyday feel better." text="Tell us how your kitchen or bathroom works today, and what you would like to be different." />
</SiteLayout>
